# Test: ze doctor refuses a config file given without the config keyword
# VALIDATES: `ze doctor <file>` exits 1 with an error naming the grammar
# `ze doctor config <file>`, and runs no readiness check (no JSON verdict on
# stdout). The accepted form `ze doctor config <file>` is what every other
# doctor-*.ci runs.
# PREVENTS: a free-form path in the first slot after the noun (ai/rules/cli.md,
# keyword before value), which a file named `config` or `kernel-capabilities`
# would turn into a different mode.

tmpfs=empty.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
# empty config
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json empty.conf:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=ze doctor config <file>
reject=stdout:contains="ready"
